# Claude Code workspace — session state + worktrees. The worktrees
# directory alone is ~hundreds of MB of repo clones, which floods
# the IDE source-control panel with phantom "untracked" entries.
.claude/

# `docs/superpowers/` is the working folder for the brainstorming +
# writing-plans skills. Real design docs go under
# `docs/architecture/` (with a "Status: design" header if not yet
# shipped); plans archive with the PR on GitHub. Local drafts sit
# under `.claude/{plans,specs}/` (already ignored above).
docs/superpowers/

# uv lockfile — opted out of tracking (env-specific resolution;
# pyproject.toml is the version source of truth).
uv.lock

# Go build artifacts at repo root from `go build ./...` runs
/loom-llm-gateway-sandbox

# Operator-owned storage lifecycle config. `config/storage-lifecycle.example.toml`
# is the committed template; operators `cp` it to `config/storage-lifecycle.toml`
# and tune per-workload retention windows before running
# `loom cluster bootstrap-storage-lifecycle` (see docs/operator-runbook.md).
# The active copy is per-deployment and must not be committed.
config/storage-lifecycle.toml

